            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0556" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg428"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 307.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pendleton to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 2, 1885</date>.
                        (Received November 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 100.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith the
                    annual report of the “military cases” (prepared by Mr. Coleman, secretary of
                    legation), which have during the past year required the attention of this
                    legation and been brought to a conclusion. The inclosure embraces cases Nos.
                    107, 115, 116, 117, 118, 119, 120, 121, 122, 123, 124, 125, 126, and 128.
                    Pending cases are reserved for a subsequent report.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEOEGE H. PENDLETON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d307-a1.xml" xpointer="d307-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
